RT-DETR / RT-DETRv2 source adaptations
  Original repository: https://github.com/lyuwenyu/RT-DETR
  Authors: lyuwenyu and RT-DETR contributors
  License: Apache License 2.0 (included as munet_zoo/rtdetrv2/LICENSE-RT-DETR)
  Pinned commits: e97db5a685a874c01c7977cb3a42ab0684ea134b (rtdetrv2_pytorch) and
                  29320b6fd828f8e0987a71426cf2d961b09dfed7 (rtdetr_pytorch, ResNet backbone)

  munet_zoo/rtdetrv2/{encoder,decoder,utils,loss,denoising}.py, munet_zoo/backbones/presnet.py and ConvNormLayer in
  munet_zoo/backbones/common.py adapt the reference architecture, parameter names and loss definitions.
  Changes: PyTorch execution is replaced by MuNet graph operations; targets are padded arrays; matching runs as a
  graph operation; denoising noise is prepared on the host and passed in; initialization uses NumPy; anchors and
  sampling scales are constants instead of stored buffers; discrete sampling clamps x and y to their own extents.

ConvNeXt V2
  Architecture: Woo et al., "ConvNeXt V2: Co-designing and Scaling ConvNets with Masked Autoencoders", 2023.
  munet_zoo/backbones/convnextv2.py is written for MuNet. Its parameter names follow the timm implementation
  (https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models, Apache License 2.0) so that timm weight files load.

YOLOX
  Architecture: Ge et al., "YOLOX: Exceeding YOLO Series in 2021", 2021 (reference implementation: Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX,
  Apache License 2.0). munet_zoo/yolox is written for MuNet from the paper's design; no upstream source is included.

Pretrained weights are not part of this repository. They keep their own licenses; the ConvNeXt V2 FCMAE weights
published by Meta are CC-BY-NC-4.0 (non-commercial).
